      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well as we discussed last week there may be cases where we need long lived MSAA attachments. I wonder if this call should take a flag that say if the MSAA buffer will be used for discardable msaa or not. If not, then we have to use Private always. If so then it doesn\u0027t really matter to the callers if we pick memoryless or not. Remember memoryless is different than discardable.\n\nNow if it makes things simpler to have a cap to query memoryless support that\u0027s fine since we want to do this same query for stencil/depth as well. I think I might even consider just having a private function that is like:\nMtlStorageMode storageModeForDiscardableTexture(); (maybe that can just be static depending on the support checks we need).\n\nI\u0027ll defer to jim on the correct way to do the mix of #ifdef, if(@available), and if  (this-\u003eisMac()/isApple) checks to put in here.",
